The code uses smart pointers (unique_ptr) for managing memory, minimizing potential fragmentation issues. The splitNode() function handles dynamic resizing by recursively splitting a node when its data capacity exceeds the maximum data capacity.

The code also includes serialization/deserialization using the cereal library to allow persistent storage and efficient loading. It uses mutexes for synchronization mechanisms to prevent data corruption during concurrent access from multiple threads. However, you'll need to implement the thread-safe insertion and query functions according to your specific requirements.

