The function also validates the integrity of the linked list after all records are initialized, checking for cycles and ensuring every record is reachable from the head node using the `is_reachable()` function. The memory allocated is deallocated upon function exit.

The code has been optimized to minimize time and space complexity by using a circular linked list and optimizing the random number generation. Additionally, it follows the given constraint of being thread-safe if used in a multi-threaded environment.']

