The `process_new_data` function allows for iterating over the array and invoking an external database processing function for each element. This design accommodates high-concurrency scenarios, but developers should evaluate trade-offs between memory usage, concurrency overhead, and performance when selecting the synchronization method (e.g., mutexes, condition variables).

