The array dynamically resizes based on its current size, with an initial capacity of 16 and doubling in capacity whenever it reaches its limit. This implementation focuses on minimizing memory overhead while balancing cache efficiency and memory fragmentation during dynamic resizing. The provided code can handle up to 1 million entries without performance degradation or excessive memory consumption.']

