        serialize(structure, buffer + ret, MAX_STRUCTURES * SERIALIZED_SIZE - ret);
        ret += SERIALIZED_SIZE;
    }
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&pool->lock);

    // Implement network transmission here (e.g., sockets)
    if (ret < 0) {
        free(buffer);
        return -1;
    }

    ret = send(destination, buffer, ret, 0);
    free(buffer);
    return ret >= 0 ? 0 : -1;
}
```

This code provides a basic implementation of the task description. It creates a memory pool for LTE UE context management structures, handles concurrent access using a mutex lock, and includes serialization functionality for transmission over a network interface. Error handling and logging are implemented using `snprintf`. The example uses a simple function for serializing the context structure; you may replace it with your chosen serialization format.

To minimize contention and potential deadlocks or race conditions, use the provided mutex lock when modifying the pool and its structures. Evaluate other locking mechanisms based on specific threading requirements in your application.']

